From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: Release a parser's elements once after a failed connect.

wg_parser_connect() releases my_src and the container when it fails, leaving
my_src set, and DirectShow then calls wg_parser_disconnect(). It released
my_src again and used the NULL container. The double release corrupts memory, and a
game that retries a graph it cannot build is aborted by GLib after some minutes.

---

diff --git a/dlls/winegstreamer/wg_parser.c b/dlls/winegstreamer/wg_parser.c
--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/wg_parser.c
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/wg_parser.c
@@ -1830,7 +1830,10 @@
     if (parser->container)
         gst_element_set_state(parser->container, GST_STATE_NULL);
     if (parser->my_src)
+    {
         gst_object_unref(parser->my_src);
+        parser->my_src = NULL;
+    }
 
     for (i = 0; i < parser->stream_count; ++i)
         free_stream(parser->streams[i]);
@@ -1872,6 +1875,13 @@
     struct wg_parser *parser = get_parser(*(wg_parser_t *)args);
     unsigned int i;
 
+    /* A connect that failed has already released all of this. */
+    if (!parser->container)
+    {
+        parser_clear_input_cache(parser);
+        return S_OK;
+    }
+
     /* Unblock all of our streams. */
     pthread_mutex_lock(&parser->mutex);
     for (i = 0; i < parser->stream_count; ++i)
